---
import IndustryVisaPage from '../components/IndustryVisaPage.astro';
---
<IndustryVisaPage
  title="Visas for Performers, Musicians & Touring Crews | Unique Visa Services"
  description="Visas for UK musicians, performers, dancers and touring crews performing overseas. Group applications for bands, productions and their crew."
  crumb="Performers and touring"
  h1="Visas for Performers, Musicians and Touring Crews"
  intro="Performing abroad, even for one night, often counts as work. We help musicians, performers and their crews get the right visas for every country on the tour."
  who={[
    "Bands, musicians and DJs playing overseas",
    "Theatre, dance and circus productions on tour",
    "Comedians and speakers performing at international events",
    "Touring crew: sound, lighting, stage management and tour managers",
  ]}
  visas={[
    ["Performer or entertainment visa", "Concerts, festivals and shows in countries with a specific visa for performers"],
    ["Work visa or permit", "Paid performances in countries without a dedicated performer visa"],
    ["Business visa", "Promotional meetings and some unpaid showcases, where the country allows it"],
  ]}
  sections={[
    { h: "Touring several countries", p: [
      "Every country on a tour can have different rules, timings and fees. We map out the visas for the whole route and plan the applications so passports are free when each one is needed.",
    ]},
    { h: "Performing in the USA", p: [
      "Performers usually need a US work visa, which starts with a petition to US immigration authorities before the visa interview. That petition is normally handled by a US immigration lawyer. We can work alongside your lawyer on the visa application and appointment stage, and tell you clearly what we handle and what we refer on.",
    ]},
  ]}
  checklist={[
    "Passports for all performers and crew",
    "Performance contracts or letters from the venue or promoter",
    "Tour itinerary with dates and venues",
    "Crew list with names and roles",
    "Proof of professional standing, such as press or past performances, where required",
  ]}
  faqs={[
    { q: "Do I need a visa for a one-off gig abroad?", a: "Often yes. Many countries treat any paid performance as work, even a single show. We check each country on your schedule." },
    { q: "Do you handle US performer visas?", a: "US performer visas need a petition first, usually handled by a US immigration lawyer. We can help with the later visa stages and work alongside your lawyer." },
    { q: "Can crew travel on the same visa as the performers?", a: "It depends on the country. Some cover essential crew under the same category, others need separate applications. We'll confirm for each destination." },
  ]}
  related={[["Film and TV crew visas", "/film-tv-crew-visas/"], ["USA visa services", "/usa-visa-services/"]]}
/>
